WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:08.346
Hi! Today we'll discover a secret: division and fractions are really the same thing!

2
00:00:08.496 --> 00:00:13.746
At a garden picnic, there are 3 pies to share equally among 4 children.

3
00:00:13.896 --> 00:00:21.042
Each child can't get a whole pie, so we cut each pie into 4 pieces. Each piece is one quarter.

4
00:00:21.192 --> 00:00:26.610
Each child takes one piece from each pie, so each child gets 3 quarters.

5
00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:36.930
So 3 divided by 4 equals three quarters. The number being divided goes on top, and the number we divide by goes at the bottom.

6
00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:42.786
We can also write a fraction as a decimal. What is three quarters as a decimal?

7
00:00:42.936 --> 00:00:50.490
Make the denominator 100. Multiply the top and bottom by 25 to get 75 hundredths.

8
00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:54.762
75 hundredths is 0.75.

9
00:00:54.912 --> 00:01:02.802
Now try seven fifths. Multiply the top and bottom by 2 to get 14 tenths, which is 1.4.

10
00:01:02.952 --> 00:01:10.362
Or we can just work out 7 divided by 5. The answer is still 1.4.

11
00:01:10.512 --> 00:01:17.346
One more: 2 litres of juice are shared equally among 5 cups. How much is in each cup?

12
00:01:17.496 --> 00:01:21.330
2 divided by 5 is 2 fifths of a litre.

13
00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:28.722
Multiply the top and bottom by 2 to get 4 tenths, which is 0.4 litres.

14
00:01:28.872 --> 00:01:35.730
Watch out! Some pupils write 3 divided by 4 as four thirds. That is wrong!

15
00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:43.146
The 3 is being divided, so it goes on top. The 4 goes at the bottom. It is three quarters.

16
00:01:43.296 --> 00:01:50.178
Check: 3 pies shared by 4 children must be less than one pie each.

17
00:01:50.328 --> 00:02:00.234
Your turn! Write 9 divided by 4 as a fraction and as a decimal. Pause and think.

18
00:02:00.384 --> 00:02:10.866
9 divided by 4 is nine quarters, which is 2 and 1 quarter. As a decimal, that is 2.25. Did you get it right?

19
00:02:11.016 --> 00:02:20.250
Another one! Write 7 divided by 20 as a decimal. Pause and think.

20
00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:33.234
7 divided by 20 is 7 twentieths. Multiply the top and bottom by 5 to get 35 hundredths, which is 0.35. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:33.384 --> 00:02:42.426
Last one! Write 11 divided by 4 as a decimal. Pause and think.

22
00:02:42.576 --> 00:02:54.498
11 divided by 4 is 2 and 3 quarters. 3 quarters is 0.75, so the answer is 2.75. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:54.648 --> 00:03:03.522
Remember: a divided by b is a over b. To get a decimal, make the denominator 10 or 100, or simply divide.

24
00:03:03.672 --> 00:03:07.866
Now go and practise in your garden!

